11 of 15. A customer who has bought from you for 5 years, or someone buying one of your special products, spends ₹5,000. Do they earn more points than a new customer?
  A) No: everybody earns at the same rate  B) Regular or VIP customers earn extra (for example 1.5 times the points)  C) Certain products earn double points, as chosen by you
  Your answer (a letter, or your own words) > 
  > A) No: everybody earns at the same rate. I only give one point for every full ₹100 of items paid, after the discount code, with the other rules I already told you (₹500 minimum, no points on store credit, double points on final-sale orders).

12 of 15. On your daily sales summary, there are 10 orders: 7 paid, 1 cancelled, 1 refunded after delivery, and 1 not yet paid. Which count?
  A) Only paid, non-cancelled orders; refunded amounts are subtracted from revenue  B) All orders placed that day, whatever happened to them  C) Only paid orders; refunds are ignored until the day they are processed in a separate report
  Your answer (a letter, or your own words) > 
